window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-034.json",{"day":34,"title":"Reading a Lake Before Restoring It","targetWords":[{"word":"disperse","gloss":"分散","context":"Evidence showed that fertilizers could deplete oxygen, while storm runoff might erode the banks and disperse sediment.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"erode","gloss":"侵蚀","context":"Evidence showed that fertilizers could deplete oxygen, while storm runoff might erode the banks and disperse sediment.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"blend","gloss":"混合","context":"Chemicals could diffuse through shallow water or blend with material carried from farms.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"deplete","gloss":"耗尽","context":"Evidence showed that fertilizers could deplete oxygen, while storm runoff might erode the banks and disperse sediment.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"transcend","gloss":"超越","context":"The project also had to transcend narrow institutional interests.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"ascend","gloss":"上升","context":"A year later, birds began to ascend above clearer water and evening light seemed to radiate across the shore.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"radiate","gloss":"散开","context":"A year later, birds began to ascend above clearer water and evening light seemed to radiate across the shore.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"segregate","gloss":"隔离","context":"If they tried to segregate the lake from its surrounding land, the plan would miss the processes that connect them.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"diffuse","gloss":"弥漫","context":"Chemicals could diffuse through shallow water or blend with material carried from farms.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"eradicate","gloss":"根除","context":"Engineers proposed to dilute some contaminants and eradicate an invasive plant, but no single treatment would suffice.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"amend","gloss":"修正","context":"As floodwater began to recede, teams could amend sampling procedures.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"suffice","gloss":"足够","context":"Engineers proposed to dilute some contaminants and eradicate an invasive plant, but no single treatment would suffice.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"dilute","gloss":"稀释","context":"Engineers proposed to dilute some contaminants and eradicate an invasive plant, but no single treatment would suffice.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"propagate","gloss":"传播","context":"A department might propagate an appealing story to protect its reputation, while another could suppose that delay was someone else's fault.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"recede","gloss":"后退","context":"As floodwater began to recede, teams could amend sampling procedures.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"stagnate","gloss":"停滞不前","context":"Such habits would let cooperation stagnate and eventually degenerate into blame.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"degenerate","gloss":"退化","context":"Such habits would let cooperation stagnate and eventually degenerate into blame.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"question","gloss":"问题","context":"When researchers reached a polluted lake, their first question was not which machine to buy.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"say","gloss":"说","context":"The public meeting required researchers to say what they could and could not conclude.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"follow","gloss":"追踪","context":"Residents would pay part of the cost, so they deserved to attend the discussion and follow the evidence.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"read","gloss":"读","context":"An older fisherman invited them to read notebooks recording catches across thirty years.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"think","gloss":"认为","context":"The coordinator urged teams to think across boundaries and imagine how decisions would affect people outside their own offices.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"know","gloss":"知道","context":"They wanted to know how the water had changed and what local residents could remember.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pay","gloss":"支付","context":"Residents would pay part of the cost, so they deserved to attend the discussion and follow the evidence.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"believe","gloss":"相信","context":"Scientists could not simply persuade everyone to believe them; they had to explain why particular observations mattered.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"allow","gloss":"允许","context":"A farmer asked whether the plan would allow fields to remain productive.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"decide","gloss":"决定","context":"To decide responsibly meant accepting that a convenient explanation could still be a mistake, especially when important information had not yet been collected.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"plan","gloss":"计划","context":"If they tried to segregate the lake from its surrounding land, the plan would miss the processes that connect them.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"consider","gloss":"考虑","context":"They asked participants to consider alternatives, focus on comparable measurements, and avoid treating one mistaken prediction as proof that all research was worthless.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"mind","gloss":"介意","context":"She did not mind disagreement, but she would not let participants forget the purpose of the work.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"focus","gloss":"聚焦","context":"They asked participants to consider alternatives, focus on comparable measurements, and avoid treating one mistaken prediction as proof that all research was worthless.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"depend","gloss":"依赖","context":"Trust would depend on openness about limits as well as findings.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"remember","gloss":"记得","context":"They wanted to know how the water had changed and what local residents could remember.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"determine","gloss":"查明","context":"They needed to determine whether changes reflected genuine recovery or merely a temporary shift in weather conditions.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"occur","gloss":"发生","context":"Recovery would occur through patient observation rather than celebration alone.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"attend","gloss":"出席","context":"Residents would pay part of the cost, so they deserved to attend the discussion and follow the evidence.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"mistake","gloss":"错误","context":"To decide responsibly meant accepting that a convenient explanation could still be a mistake, especially when important information had not yet been collected.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"forget","gloss":"忘记","context":"She did not mind disagreement, but she would not let participants forget the purpose of the work.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"suppose","gloss":"假设","context":"A department might propagate an appealing story to protect its reputation, while another could suppose that delay was someone else's fault.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"associate","gloss":"联系","context":"Researchers were careful not to associate every pleasant sign with their intervention or perceive a pattern where chance might be sufficient.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"observe","gloss":"观察","context":"They could observe where algae began to spread, notice when fish disappeared, and recall seasons that had once seemed exceptional.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"wonder","gloss":"思考","context":"It begins with willingness to wonder whether the most obvious account leaves out something that the people who live nearby have already learned.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"imagine","gloss":"想象","context":"The coordinator urged teams to think across boundaries and imagine how decisions would affect people outside their own offices.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"convince","gloss":"使人信服","context":"Residents could still suspect that official accounts were too optimistic, and scientists had to earn the confidence needed to convince them otherwise.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"persuade","gloss":"说服","context":"Scientists could not simply persuade everyone to believe them; they had to explain why particular observations mattered.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"notice","gloss":"注意","context":"They could observe where algae began to spread, notice when fish disappeared, and recall seasons that had once seemed exceptional.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"recall","gloss":"回想","context":"They could observe where algae began to spread, notice when fish disappeared, and recall seasons that had once seemed exceptional.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"perceive","gloss":"察觉","context":"Researchers were careful not to associate every pleasant sign with their intervention or perceive a pattern where chance might be sufficient.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"borrow","gloss":"借","context":"Another wanted to borrow equipment for independent monitoring.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"suspect","gloss":"怀疑","context":"Residents could still suspect that official accounts were too optimistic, and scientists had to earn the confidence needed to convince them otherwise.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"When researchers reached a polluted lake, their first question was not which machine to buy. They wanted to know how the water had changed and what local residents could remember. An older fisherman invited them to read notebooks recording catches across thirty years. They could observe where algae began to spread, notice when fish disappeared, and recall seasons that had once seemed exceptional. Scientific attention requires more than confidence in a familiar explanation. It begins with willingness to wonder whether the most obvious account leaves out something that the people who live nearby have already learned.","zh":"研究者来到污染湖泊时，首先问的不是买什么机器，而是水发生了哪些变化、居民记得什么。年长渔民请他们看记录三十年渔获的笔记。他们观察藻类从哪里扩散、何时鱼消失，回想过去显得异常的季节。科学注意不仅需要相信熟悉解释，更始于愿意思考：最显眼的说法是否遗漏了附近生活者早已了解的事情。"},{"en":"Evidence showed that fertilizers could deplete oxygen, while storm runoff might erode the banks and disperse sediment. Chemicals could diffuse through shallow water or blend with material carried from farms. Engineers proposed to dilute some contaminants and eradicate an invasive plant, but no single treatment would suffice. If they tried to segregate the lake from its surrounding land, the plan would miss the processes that connect them. As floodwater began to recede, teams could amend sampling procedures. They needed to determine whether changes reflected genuine recovery or merely a temporary shift in weather conditions.","zh":"证据显示，肥料可能耗尽氧气，暴雨径流侵蚀湖岸并分散沉积物。化学物可在浅水中扩散，或与农地带来的物质混合。工程师建议稀释部分污染物、清除入侵植物，但没有单项处理足够。如果试图把湖与周边土地分开看，计划就会忽略连接它们的过程。洪水退去后，团队可修订取样流程，判断变化是真正恢复，还是暂时天气转变。"},{"en":"The public meeting required researchers to say what they could and could not conclude. Residents would pay part of the cost, so they deserved to attend the discussion and follow the evidence. A farmer asked whether the plan would allow fields to remain productive. Another wanted to borrow equipment for independent monitoring. Scientists could not simply persuade everyone to believe them; they had to explain why particular observations mattered. They asked participants to consider alternatives, focus on comparable measurements, and avoid treating one mistaken prediction as proof that all research was worthless. Trust would depend on openness about limits as well as findings.","zh":"公众会议要求研究者说明能与不能得出哪些结论。居民将承担部分费用，因此应参与讨论、追踪证据。农民问计划是否允许田地保持生产，另一个想借设备独立监测。科学家不能只劝大家相信自己，必须解释特定观察为何重要。他们请参与者考虑替代解释、关注可比较测量，避免把一次预测错误当作所有研究都无价值的证据。信任既依赖公开发现，也依赖公开局限。"},{"en":"The project also had to transcend narrow institutional interests. A department might propagate an appealing story to protect its reputation, while another could suppose that delay was someone else's fault. Such habits would let cooperation stagnate and eventually degenerate into blame. The coordinator urged teams to think across boundaries and imagine how decisions would affect people outside their own offices. She did not mind disagreement, but she would not let participants forget the purpose of the work. To decide responsibly meant accepting that a convenient explanation could still be a mistake, especially when important information had not yet been collected.","zh":"项目也必须超越狭隘机构利益。一部门可能宣传讨喜故事保护声誉，另一部门可能假设延误都是别人造成。这类习惯让合作停滞，最终退化为责备。协调者促使团队跨越边界思考，想象决定对办公室之外的人有何影响。她不介意分歧，却不让参与者忘记工作目的。负责地决定，意味着承认方便解释仍可能是错误，尤其关键资料尚未收集时。"},{"en":"A year later, birds began to ascend above clearer water and evening light seemed to radiate across the shore. Researchers were careful not to associate every pleasant sign with their intervention or perceive a pattern where chance might be sufficient. Residents could still suspect that official accounts were too optimistic, and scientists had to earn the confidence needed to convince them otherwise. Recovery would occur through patient observation rather than celebration alone. The lake taught everyone a modest lesson: good decisions arise when people remain prepared to revise what they think they know, while continuing the practical work that improvement requires.","zh":"一年后，鸟在更清澈的水面上升起，暮光仿佛在岸边散开。研究者谨慎，不把每个好迹象都与干预联系，也不在偶然已足以解释时硬看出规律。居民仍可以怀疑官方过于乐观，科学家需要赢得信任才能令人信服。恢复依赖耐心观察，而非仅靠庆祝。湖泊给大家一个朴素教训：人在愿意修正自认为知道的事情，同时持续做改善所需实际工作时，才会产生好的决定。"}],"previous":33,"next":35});
